WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:14.752
Unit one: Friendship. In this unit, you will describe a good friend and what friends do for each other.

4
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.519
Trust.

5
00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:20.147
Trust means to believe that someone is honest and good.

6
00:00:20.447 --> 00:00:22.888
I trust my best friend with my secrets.

7
00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:26.542
Your turn. Say: Trust.

8
00:00:29.242 --> 00:00:30.046
Trust.

9
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:31.947
Loyal.

10
00:00:32.647 --> 00:00:35.436
Loyal means always staying with and supporting a friend.

11
00:00:35.736 --> 00:00:38.768
A loyal friend stays with you in hard times.

12
00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:42.643
Your turn. Say: Loyal.

13
00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:46.066
Loyal.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:47.958
Support.

15
00:00:48.658 --> 00:00:51.180
Support means to help someone and give them courage.

16
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.724
My friends support me before exams.

17
00:00:54.424 --> 00:00:56.983
Your turn. Say: Support.

18
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:00.591
Support.

19
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:02.526
Forgive.

20
00:01:03.226 --> 00:01:05.714
Forgive means to stop being angry with someone.

21
00:01:06.014 --> 00:01:08.654
I forgive you. Let's be friends again.

22
00:01:09.354 --> 00:01:11.426
Your turn. Say: Forgive.

23
00:01:14.126 --> 00:01:14.895
Forgive.

24
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:16.571
Share.

25
00:01:17.271 --> 00:01:19.630
Share means to give part of something to others.

26
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.663
We share our snacks at break time.

27
00:01:22.363 --> 00:01:24.551
Your turn. Say: Share.

28
00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:28.159
Share.

29
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.256
Understand.

30
00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:34.476
Understand means to know how someone feels or what they mean.

31
00:01:34.776 --> 00:01:36.590
Good friends understand each other.

32
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.221
Your turn. Say: Understand.

33
00:01:42.921 --> 00:01:44.015
Understand.

34
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:46.041
Reliable.

35
00:01:46.741 --> 00:01:49.333
Reliable means someone you can always depend on.

36
00:01:49.633 --> 00:01:52.598
Dara is reliable. He always comes on time.

37
00:01:53.298 --> 00:01:55.777
Your turn. Say: Reliable.

38
00:01:58.477 --> 00:01:59.489
Reliable.

39
00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:01.322
Honest.

40
00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:04.184
Honest means always telling the truth.

41
00:02:04.484 --> 00:02:06.646
An honest friend tells you the truth.

42
00:02:07.346 --> 00:02:10.428
Your turn. Say: Honest.

43
00:02:13.128 --> 00:02:14.083
Honest.

44
00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:16.154
Generous.

45
00:02:16.854 --> 00:02:20.293
Generous means happy to give time, money or things to others.

46
00:02:20.593 --> 00:02:22.871
My generous friend gave me her pen.

47
00:02:23.571 --> 00:02:26.282
Your turn. Say: Generous.

48
00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.960
Generous.

49
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:31.812
Encourage.

50
00:02:32.512 --> 00:02:35.545
Encourage means to say things that help someone try.

51
00:02:35.845 --> 00:02:37.763
My friends encourage me to sing.

52
00:02:38.463 --> 00:02:41.208
Your turn. Say: Encourage.

53
00:02:43.908 --> 00:02:44.909
Encourage.

54
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:47.057
Apologize.

55
00:02:47.757 --> 00:02:49.791
Apologize means to say sorry.

56
00:02:50.091 --> 00:02:51.987
I apologize for being late.

57
00:02:52.687 --> 00:02:55.931
Your turn. Say: Apologize.

58
00:02:58.631 --> 00:02:59.864
Apologize.

59
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:01.654
Reunite.

60
00:03:02.354 --> 00:03:05.352
Reunite means to meet again after a long time apart.

61
00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.394
Old classmates reunite every Khmer New Year.

62
00:03:09.094 --> 00:03:12.130
Your turn. Say: Reunite.

63
00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.947
Reunite.

64
00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.054
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:19.354 --> 00:03:22.294
Sreypich, tell me about your best friend.

66
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:26.839
Her name is Bopha. She is a friend who always supports me.

67
00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.395
Why do you trust her?

68
00:03:30.683 --> 00:03:34.067
She is honest and loyal. She never tells my secrets.

69
00:03:35.383 --> 00:03:36.640
Do you ever argue?

70
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.936
Sometimes, but we apologize and forgive each other.

71
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.039
Grammar focus: Relative pronoun who.

72
00:03:45.339 --> 00:03:47.722
A loyal friend is a person who supports you.

73
00:03:48.022 --> 00:03:50.567
Use 'who' to give more information about a person.

74
00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:54.410
Now read and listen. My Best Friend Bopha.

75
00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.000
Bopha is a friend who always supports me.

76
00:03:58.283 --> 00:04:00.840
She is honest, so I trust her with my secrets.

77
00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:06.030
Last year, we had an argument, but she apologized and I forgave her.

78
00:04:07.317 --> 00:04:09.641
She is generous and shares her books with me.

79
00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.170
We will stay loyal friends forever.

80
00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:17.124
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:19.737
A friend blank tells the truth is honest.

82
00:04:20.037 --> 00:04:23.052
A, who. B, which. C, where.

83
00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.806
The answer is A: who.

84
00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:32.014
To say sorry is to blank.

85
00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:36.293
A, apologize. B, forgive. C, reunite.

86
00:04:40.283 --> 00:04:42.329
The answer is A: apologize.

87
00:04:43.817 --> 00:04:46.234
Someone you can always depend on is blank.

88
00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:50.257
A, reliable. B, generous. C, nervous.

89
00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.551
The answer is A: reliable.

90
00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.062
Now it's your turn to speak. What makes a good friend?

91
00:05:06.362 --> 00:05:12.776
A good friend is someone who is honest and loyal. My best friend supports me, and we always forgive each other.

92
00:05:13.076 --> 00:05:15.064
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.351
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and relative pronoun who.

94
00:05:20.651 --> 00:05:25.103
Today's value is loyalty. Stand by your friends in good times and bad times.

95
00:05:25.403 --> 00:05:27.637
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

96
00:05:27.937 --> 00:05:30.682
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

